 "cells": [
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "29e15248",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# Simple Powder Diffractometer testing\n",
    "The classic McStas `.instr` format can be converted with the McStasScript python API, which allows you to make a widget that can run the simulation for you. The conversion tool is called `mcstas-pygen`, so for this instrument I've called:\n",
    "```\n",
    "mcstas-pygen SimplePowderDiffractometer.instr\n",
    "```\n",
    "Which generated `SimplePowderDiffractometer_generated.py`, that can be directly imported into a Jupyter notebook. \n",
    "\n",
    "The converted instrument file does not currently automatically get the instrument parameter descriptions from the `.instr` file, so those have been edited manually into the `_generated.py` instrument. There are different keyword arguments that can also be added for the parameters in there: for example you can use the `options` keyword to add a dropdown menu for one of the parameters.\n",
    "\n",
    "Further documentation about widgets can be found on: https://panosc-vinyl.github.io/McStasScript/user_guide/widgets.html\n",
    "\n",
    "### Hiding some of the code in a subfolder \n",
    "All the necessary code is placed in `code_folder`, to hide some of the complexity that is not necessary for students to understand during our simulation quizzes. Datafiles will still be written to this directory, so they can be fetched and worked with in different data processing software, if you so wish.\n",
    "\n\n",
    "Now, let us move on to the loading of the instrument into this notebook, and then opening up the widget to run the instrument:\n",
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "b7ce66c1",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# First, load in the exercise python code, which in turn reads in the instrument\n",
    "import code_folder.exercise as exercise"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "3302717f",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "![Sketch](code_folder/SimplePowderDiffractometer.png)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "5190963b",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Show the instrument with the widget, so we can run the instrument with the different defined parameters\n",
    "%matplotlib widget\n",
    "sim_interface = exercise.make_widget_interface()\n",
    "sim_interface.show_interface()\n",
    "\n",
    "# After setting the wanted parameters, hit the Run button to run the simulation, then choose a monitor to view data\n",
    "# You can also set mpi=4, to use all 4 cores of the virtual machine"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "7778ac53",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Visualize instrument"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "3c2eab9e",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "sim_interface.instrument.show_instrument(backend=\"pythreejs\")"
   ]
  },
